# Task 4 — `doc-composer` seat + guardrail routing (spec 40, design §4.4)

Executor: architect (Claude). D-rung: D3 (live invoke via deployed invoker).

## What shipped

- `services/ai-invoker/src/types.ts` — `SeatId`/`SeatTier` += `'doc-composer'`;
  `SEAT_DEFAULTS['doc-composer'] = { temperature: 0.2, maxTokens: 4096 }`;
  `ContentBlock` += `{ guardedText }` (see live defect below).
- `services/ai-invoker/src/doc-composer-schema.ts` — `DOC_COMPOSER_OUTPUT_SCHEMA`
  `{sentences:[{text, factRefs[]}]}` + `DocComposerOutput` type, exported from the
  invoker index for ComposeSection (Task 5). Shape only — fact RESOLUTION stays in
  the deterministic checker (BC-4: the model never grades itself).
- `services/ai-invoker/src/guardrail.ts` — `buildGuardrailConfig(seat)`:
  `doc-composer` → `DOCGEN_GUARDRAIL_*`, every other seat → agent guardrail.
  If `DOCGEN_GUARDRAIL_ID` is unset the seat gets NO guardrail rather than
  falling back to the agent guardrail (a fallback would silently anonymize
  tenant names out of generated manuals — the exact ACC-9 failure).
- Register ×3 in lockstep (drift test enforces): `contracts/model-register.md`
  appended Doc-Composer entry (`us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0`, PROVISIONAL — golden-set
  eval ≥4.0/5 at Task 12, owner ratifies there); `compile-register.ts` SEAT_MAP;
  `register-compiled.json` regenerated (11 seats); drift-test SEAT_NAME_TO_ID.
- MODELWEIGHT#: keyed by modelId, NOT seat — nova-pro row pre-exists (workhorse/
  editor-ai). No new row needed; pinned by test so a future model change without
  a weights row fails the suite before it fails `loadWeights` in production.
- `schema-retry.ts` — validator deepened from top-level-only to recursive
  (type/required/properties/items/minItems/minLength/additionalProperties:false).
  The old check silently PASSED sentences missing factRefs — caught by the new
  rejection tests. No existing caller regressed (no agent declares an
  outputSchema today; tool-loop passes it through).
- Tests: `guardrail.test.ts` (routing pinned BOTH directions incl. all 10 agent
  seats), `doc-composer-seat.test.ts` (register entry, defaults, weights row,
  schema accept/reject ×5), converse guardContent mapping test.

## Live defect found & fixed (the reason readbacks exercise behavior)

First live invoke: `guardrail_intervened`, text "Request blocked by content
policy.", credits 0. Isolation (exp1/exp2): plain prose request PASSES with
names intact; adding the strict JSON-format instruction ("Respond with ONLY a
JSON object … and nothing else") trips PROMPT_ATTACK at input HIGH. Every
production doc-composer prompt needs a format instruction → seat would be
unusable at HIGH; lowering the filter was rejected (the injection surface —
tenant-entered field values — is exactly what it must keep guarding).

Fix: Bedrock **selective guardrail evaluation** — new `guardedText` content
block mapped to Converse `guardContent`. When present, input policies evaluate
ONLY those blocks: our scaffolding (format instruction) rides unevaluated,
tenant-sourced facts stay fully guarded, PROMPT_ATTACK stays HIGH.
**Task 5 contract: ComposeSection MUST wrap every tenant-sourced fact in
`guardedText` and keep its own scaffolding in plain `text` blocks.**

